+## Path-fix option "geometry": set and people share one height scale
+
+`lib/room.ts` changes (plan x, z untouched; the optics model and lib/optics are untouched):
+- `PARTITION_H = 2.0`: the partition's drawn height (layout.json keeps the research value 1.7 m). It is the tallest screen whose arched top still fits CAM_ROOM at tilt 0.
+- `LIGHT_H = 0.95`: the drawn height of the light paths' plane (S, the wall samples, his torso point H). All three share it, so plan lengths stay exact 3D lengths. On the chibi rig, 1.2 m is the chin; 0.95 m is the chest.
+- `LAYOUT` (room.ts only) carries both overrides, so `PTS`, `occluderBox`, `<Partition>`, `<RoomSet>` and every scene's `SENSOR_H = LAYOUT.sensor.h` use them.
+- `rigScale(s, heightM)` (new): `heightM * ppm * height / RIG_PX`. `rigAt` uses it, so a rig shrinks uniformly with the set's height scale as the camera rises (0.71x at RAISED_TILT). It is never squashed, and a 1.7 m person matches 1.7 m of wall or partition at every tilt. `depthSort`'s billboard rectangles, `<PottedPlant>` and S9's `walkAt` use the same scale.
+- Horizontal reaches grow in rig units as the rig shrinks, so check reach2 contacts at the raised tilt.
